            instructions: "The Labyrinth consists of floors of skilling and combat challenges. Each run costs 1 entry. 1 entry regenerates every 2-3 days depending on cooldown upgrades.<ul><li><bold>Recommended:</bold> Levels in many different skills and combat styles to attempt at least half of the room types to effectively run the Labyrinth.</li><li><bold>Floors & Rooms:</bold> Each floor is a grid of rooms. Clear rooms to reveal adjacent ones and find the floor exit to advance. Difficulty increases as you advance through more floors.</li><li><bold>Pathing:</bold> Click rooms to queue a path. Rooms are automatically challenged in order. Drag to select multiple rooms at once.</li><li><bold>Room Types:</bold> Skilling rooms challenge one of 10 non-combat skills. Combat rooms pit you against one of 10 labyrinth monsters. Treasure rooms grant item rewards. The floor exit grants larger rewards and unlocks the next floor.</li><li><bold>Torches:</bold> One torch is consumed per room entered. Produced with Crafting.</li><li><bold>Shrouds:</bold> Instantly clear a visible challenge room without receiving XP or rewards from it. Produced with Tailoring.</li><li><bold>Beacons:</bold> Reveal hidden rooms in an area. Produced with Cheesesmithing.</li><li><bold>Crates:</bold> Grant buffs that last the entire run. One crate of each type is consumed on entry. Tea and Coffee Crates are produced with Brewing, Food Crates with Cooking.</li><li><bold>Rewards:</bold> Earn Labyrinth Tokens, Purdora's Boxes, Labyrinth Refinement Chests (Floor 6+), and XP in the relevant skill. Rewards increase with floor level. Spend tokens in the Labyrinth Shop on upgrades and items.</li><li><bold>Automation:</bold> Set loadouts that will be automatically equipped for different room types and auto-skip thresholds. Upgrade Full Automation from the shop to auto-path through floors.</li></ul>",
